survey swil1d
#Data from Willie Stanton's Survey Book 1
# p. 51-52	(=PDF p.55-56)

#Typed in by Footleg, June 2012

#2nd April 1952	Cono & Roy Blewett
#Double Pots to Tratman's Temple

centreline
cs OSGB:ST 
#Resurveyed by Footleg's DblPotsDownstream and BarnesLoopToTratmans surveys, so these legs are kept
#only to connect the rest of the Stanton survey and are not counted in the length.
flags duplicate
date 1952.04.02
# Stanton's bearings come out 3 degrees clockwise of the resurvey even after
# the magnetic declination Therion works out for the date. Measured on his
# streamway books (swildons1-c, d and e, 1952-53) against the resurvey there,
# where it is the same for all three; assumed for his other books.
calibrate compass 3    # back bearings too

#in this survey some angles are in degrees:minutes, others decimal degrees
units tape feet
units depth feet

data normal from to tape compass backcompass clino ignoreall						
AL	AN	12.8	-	126:40	-4:30	AL is start of St. Pauls survey
AN	AO	16.8	025:20	-	26:00	AN is at S. end of lower big pot.
AO	AP	27.7	-	243:50	12:00	
AP	AQ	23.2	094:00	-	10:30	
AQ	AR	10.7	-	316:00	-5:30	
AR	AS	26.5	012:20	-	28:30	
AS	AT	38.6	-	169:30	10:30	
AT	AU	23.3	321:40	-	-4:00	
AU	AV	23.3	-	245:30	9:00	
AV	AW	24.1	108:30	-	27:30	AV is in middle of upper big pot.
AW	AX	14.6	-	259:40	23:30	
AX	AY	15	128:00	-	13:30	AY is on stumpy stalagmite on cascade on E side of passage.
#	AY					Total = 2,188'

endcentreline

endsurvey